I'm trying to handle these files one by one and I encountered an issue for the first one 
```
source_map_enclosing_function.js,
source_map_enclosing_function.out,
```
The `.snapshot` file is autogenerated successfully and Git detects the `.snapshot` as renamed.

The issue is, for the file `source_map_enclosing_function.js`, Git detects it as deleted and a new file even though they are very similar.

Git status:
<img width="1359" alt="image" src="https://github.com/nodejs/node/assets/42398651/26dc05c0-2a06-4a3b-8728-965d2e93f758">

The original version of `source_map_enclosing_function.js`
```js
// Flags:  --enable-source-maps

'use strict';
require('../common');
Error.stackTraceLimit = 5;

require('../fixtures/source-map/enclosing-call-site-min.js');
```
Modified version:
```js
// Flags:  --enable-source-maps

'use strict';
require('../../../common');
Error.stackTraceLimit = 5;

require('../enclosing-call-site-min.js');
```
Should I adjust the similarity index of `git diff` to modify the git rename threshold? Or should I maintain the current file status? Based on the previous discussion, I understand that we want to keep the PR with a minimal diff.
@reporter
